It was 11:47 PM when the Datadog alert came in. API latency on /checkout had SELECT pid, state, EXTRACT(EPOCH FROM (now() - query_start)) AS seconds, query FROM pg_stat_activity WHERE state != 'idle' ORDER BY query_start;
Then I ran it. Then I ran it again six seconds later. Then again. Then I SELECT * FROM pg_locks because I was Every Postgres operator has been here. The data you need lives in system pg_stat_activity, pg_locks, pg_statio_user_tables, pg_stat_user_tables. Reaching for them through a shell at midnight is a So I built the Connection Health Monitor into data-peek.
The Health Monitor is a dedicated tab — not a modal, not a sidebar — that Active Queries — everything in pg_stat_activity that isn't idle, with duration, wait events, and a kill button next to each row. Table Size…
